WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.372
A complex problem can be broken into steps.

2
00:00:03.372 --> 00:00:05.727
Those steps consume time and compute.

3
00:00:05.727 --> 00:00:07.447
And they can fail.

4
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:20.277
At inference time, you can spend more steps, samples, verification or tool interactions.

5
00:00:20.277 --> 00:00:25.171
On some tasks that can improve the answer, but it also increases cost and latency.

6
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.372
First: what reasoning means for an LLM.

7
00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:40.410
Second: how these systems fail.

8
00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:43.082
Third: how to use more inference-time compute.

9
00:00:43.082 --> 00:00:46.389
Fourth: what happens to latency and streaming.

10
00:00:46.389 --> 00:00:49.061
Fifth: when more reasoning introduces new risks.

11
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.690
More reasoning can improve quality on suitable tasks.

12
00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:04.044
It also consumes time, compute and money.

13
00:01:04.044 --> 00:01:07.669
And it can introduce overthinking, errors or new attack surfaces.
